    delphi:hasConfidence "0.77"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Modern geometry can test the critical descriptive premise and periodic crystals indeed constrain rotational symmetry. Available 3D coverage is uncertain, and the broader mechanistic exclusion is less direct than the morphological test." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Measure face, edge and angle equality in 3D polyhedral radiolarian specimens to determine whether regular dodecahedra and icosahedra truly occur. If regularity is confirmed, compare the structure with crystallographic periodic tessellation predictions, while distinguishing crystal lattice formation from broader space-partitioning mechanisms." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Haeckel's drawings may idealize specimen geometry.", "Noncrystallographic dodecahedra do not exclude every space-partitioning process." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch09-17--gpt--dataset-1> .
